{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["אכן יש ה׳ במקום הזה — Not as I thought when I lay down here, that it was a profane place, but so it is, that it is a holy place. And so too every אכן in Scripture means 'but so' — and not as I had thought. And likewise: אכן נודע הדבר."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "Rashbam writes ה׳ (with a holam) for the divine name; per the voice rules, reverent abbreviations ה׳/ד׳ are rendered HaShem. The closing quotation אכן נודע הדבר (2 Samuel 14:20) is left unaddressed as is his custom."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:45:34.739036652Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}